## Mathematical scope retained

The dimensional direct lower event is reviewed at each FIXED dimension d>=2,
fixed torus and compact birth/positive-gap ranges: 1-p_r>=c r^3 under the original
full determinant tilt and ordinary elder selector. Two extra index-(d-1) window
points give a multiple-occurrence and factorial LOWER bound. N_r can be the
torus-wide additional count; the event also supplies the same lower bound for
the deterministic C_d r ball. No higher-dimensional global first-moment upper
bound or conditional nonuniqueness lower constant is inferred.

The two-sided selection order, compact-mark density loss and rejected-pair
inverse-lifetime boundary p<5/3 are separately sourced compositions with LP's
reconciled upper/density inputs. Positive-length mark windows are required for
positive integrated coefficients. No numerical constant/cutoff, uniform-in-d
estimate or unrestricted-mark difference is introduced.

C3's reviewed claim is the fixed-remote, fixed-positive-volume Borel-region
ordered factorial-pair mean r^5 coefficient, positive precisely for adjacent
indices, and its factorial-weighted height-gap Beta(2/3,2) limit. This is not
an event-conditioned pair law or a persistence-lifetime distribution. The full
endpoint-only normalizer comes from RM; the endpoint weight limit under EXTRA
pair conditioning uses RP's coupled moments and RM's deterministic pin identities.
The unconditioned D1 normalizer theorem alone is not that extra-conditioned argument.

